<title>USA: TABLE - Int'l Nursing Services Q2 shr loss.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Int'l Nursing Services Q2 shr loss.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the three months ended June 29,</p>
<p>			     1997			1996</p>
<p>Shr loss		     0.01   loss	     0.01</p>
<p>Net loss		  101,000   loss	   61,000</p>
<p>Revs		    6,961,000		 3,216,000</p>
<p>6 MONTHS</p>
<p>Shr loss		     0.10   profit	   0.09</p>
<p>Net loss		  725,000   profit	  5,000</p>
<p>Revs		   13,624,000		 6,580,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Company said increase in revenues for the second quarter and six months of 1997 was primarily due to the acquisitions of Ellis Health Services Inc, STAT Healthg Care Services Inc in 1996 and TherAmerica earlier in 1997. While the acquisitions provided revenues of $4.2 million, however, these were offset by revenue shortfalls in Texas and Colorado due to increased compeittion and administrative personnel departures, it said.</p>
<p>Full company name is International Nursing Services Inc.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
